**6a, D-93 revised (`offer_unavailable` notice in the bar):** source `ui-screens/faster-signin-offer/faster-signin-offer.html`: screen unchanged (tile and three points); warning notice `alert-triangle` / `unlock.unavailable` in the bar slot; Turn on reads **Continue** (`offer.continue`); Not now hidden; top-of-panel notice removed; phone Back (Escape) = Continue. App `faster-signin-offer.js/.css` matches it (notice table entry `unavailable`; the primary runs Continue → Home). app-logic §2 (offer outcomes and the A-19 placement paragraph), state-map row `offer.unavailable`, `layout_check.py --app` (`#turn-on`), F5d rewritten (F5 / F5e pass). Picture rendered at 390 / 360 into `session-6/d93/`. Built app = picture, 0 px at both widths. The other six offer states are pixel-identical (12 / 12, pre-edit vs edited source). Against the approved concept at 390: same layout, 0 shifted rows, 0 bands, 0 moved regions, 0 flat-area changes; 11,396 edge pixels differ, which is above the 3,000 limit and listed in `d93/README.md`. They are spread over the unchanged title and points too, so they come from the concept's own capture route. Pushed as checkpoint 6a.

